                <pb facs="0579" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg507"/>

                <head>No. 313.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Wallace</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-05-12"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 12,
                        1882</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 56.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Acknowledging the receipt of your dispatch,
                    No. 74, of March 21 last, I have to approve your therein reported action in
                    addressing to the Turkish Government a further note in relation to the excessive
                    collections of duty upon American alcohol.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
